{"n": 660, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "660.webp", "text": "3441100 REMOVING AND INSTALLING\nPARKING BRAKE CABLE\n~ Rear Disc Brakes —\n\nRemove expansion lock for parking brake\nshoes — see 34 41 250.\n\nRemove parking brake lever — see 34 41 000.\nInstallation:\n\nAdjust parking brake — see 34 10014.\n\nDisconnect parking brake cable on swing\n\narm.\n\nPull parking brake cable out of protective\npipe,\n\nInstallation:\n\nCable holder must bear on the protective pipe,\n\nUnscrew support for parking brake cable.\nPull out parking brake cable.\n\n30 34 126\n\n34 41200 REMOVING AND INSTALLING\nPARKING BRAKE SHOES\n\nRemove rear brake disc see 34 21 300.\nDisconnect lower return spring with a brake\nspring pliers.\n\nInstallation:\n\nCheck return spring, replacing if necessary\nAdjust parking brake — see 34 10 014\n\nTurn spring retainers 90° with Special Toot\n34 4.000 and disconnect.\n\nSpread brake shoes apart at bottom and lift out\n\nfrom above.\n\nParking Brake Breaking-in Program After\n\nReplacing Liners\n\nCar must be broken in in three phases.\n\nPhase 1: Car stopped 5 times from 50 km/h\n(30 mph) with max. deceleration,\n\nPhase 2: Brakes cooled off.\n\nPhase 3: Car stopped 5 more times from\n50 km/h (30 mph)\n\n3441250 CHECKING / REMOVING AND\nINSTALLING EXPANSION LOCK\n\nRemove parking brake shoes see 34 41 200\nPull off part A toward rear\n\nPress out pin B.\n\nPull out part C.\n\nInstallation\n\nApply a thin coat of Molykote Paste G on\nsliding surfaces and pin\n\nAdjust parking brake - see 34 10 014", "words": [["3441100", 0.2619, 0.069, 0.3116, 0.0796], ["REMOVING", 0.3252, 0.069, 0.3845, 0.0796], ["AND", 0.3886, 0.069, 0.4124, 0.0796], ["INSTALLING", 0.4169, 0.069, 0.4838, 0.0796], ["PARKING", 0.3242, 0.0849, 0.3744, 0.0955], ["BRAKE", 0.3794, 0.0809, 0.4139, 0.1015], ["CABLE", 0.42, 0.0836, 0.4554, 0.0955], ["~", 0.3252, 0.1074, 0.3283, 0.1088], ["Rear", 0.3359, 0.1008, 0.3571, 0.1121], ["Disc", 0.3607, 0.1008, 0.3804, 0.1121], ["Brakes", 0.3845, 0.